## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

The connector inline HTTP client stores timeout=10.0 (c2c_relay_connector.ml:1829-1838) but request (1967-1986) calls Cohttp_lwt_unix.Client.call with no deadline - the field is dead, so any request can hang until the process SIGALRM (which then costs the hang-class ticket). The inline client also lacks C2C_RELAY_CA_BUNDLE support that relay_client.ml:196-214 has (net_ctx_of_bundle): a connector pointed at a self-signed/Tailscale HTTPS relay fails every op with connection_error while c2c doctor --relay on the same host succeeds - a confusing permanent wedge.

## Fix direction

Honor timeout (per-call deadline; note the nested Lwt_main.run constraint around line 3087) and port ca_bundle custom-ctx support.

## Evidence

Connector review 2026-09-17.